Package: com.max.xios
Name: Xios
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Section: Desktop
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 16.0), iosc (>= 0.9.39)
Breaks: xios-launcher-tools (<< 0.1.11)
MinimumOSVersion: 16.0.0
Description: the display app for the Xios desktop
 The one app iOS sees. It shows on the Home Screen as "X11", owns a Metal layer
 and the UIKit input surface, and renders nothing of its own: a GPU compositor
 hands it an output IOSurface over a mach port, the app draws that as a Metal
 texture every frame, and your touches and keystrokes go back to the server.
 Fullscreen desktop flavors need it.
 .
 It opens to a launcher: a card for each desktop that is running, with a
 thumbnail, its state and size. Tap a card to go full screen, touch and hold
 for Stop, Open app in it or Change size, and use New Desktop to start another.
 Inside a desktop, a three-finger tap or a pull from the top edge opens the
 switcher, pinch zooms, and a swipe up from the lower edge raises the keyboard.
 Several desktops can run side by side (xios-session 1.0.81, iosc 0.9.49).
 .
 Install a flavor rather than this package on its own: xios-gnome, xios-kde,
 or xios-x11. Each one pulls this app in through xios-core. The per-app native
 flavor uses xios-runtime and does not install this fullscreen display app.
 .
 Requires AppSync Unified (install it from the https://cydia.akemi.ai/ repo) to
 run this unsigned app. Rootless (/var/jb) jailbreaks only, iOS/iPadOS 16+.
